## CHAPTER 6: MEMORY ARCHITECTURE & DATABASE SCHEMA (SQLITE 3-TIER + CONVERSATIONS)

### 6.1 Database Infrastructure
- Database Engine: SQLite 3.
- Database File Location: `~/.iris/memory.db` (located at `C:\Users\<User>\.iris\memory.db`).
- Security Encryption: Field-level AES-256 encryption (`cryptography.fernet`) for deep permanent memories, backed by a persistent secret key file at `~/.iris/secret.key`.

### 6.2 The 3-Tier Core Memory Hierarchy
1. Tier 1: Temporary Memories (`temp_memories` table):
   - Purpose: Ephemeral context, active working thoughts, short-term session data.
   - Time-To-Live (TTL): 48 hours.
   - Columns: `key` (TEXT PK), `content` (TEXT), `timestamp` (REAL), `mention_count` (INTEGER), `metadata` (TEXT).
2. Tier 2: Long Temporary Memories (`long_temp_memories` table):
   - Purpose: Project tasks, ongoing todo items, active reminders, multi-day context.
   - Time-To-Live (TTL): 18 days.
   - Columns: `key` (TEXT PK), `content` (TEXT), `first_seen` (REAL), `timestamp` (REAL), `mention_count` (INTEGER), `metadata` (TEXT).
3. Tier 3: Deep Permanent Memories (`deep_memories` table):
   - Purpose: Core user identity, relationships, Commander preferences, critical facts.
   - Time-To-Live (TTL): Permanent (infinite retention).
   - Security: Encrypted at rest via AES-256 Fernet cipher.
   - Columns: `key` (TEXT PK), `content` (TEXT - encrypted), `timestamp` (REAL), `mention_count` (INTEGER), `metadata` (TEXT).

### 6.3 Multi-Conversation Database Schema
To support independent conversation sessions, two dedicated relational tables exist in SQLite:
1. `conversations` Table:
   - `id` (TEXT PRIMARY KEY): Unique identifier (`conv_<hex12>`).
   - `title` (TEXT NOT NULL): Conversation title or topic name.
   - `person_name` (TEXT): Name of the individual for dedicated person chats (e.g., "Kannaya"). Null for general topics.
   - `system_prompt` (TEXT): Custom system persona or instruction for this thread.
   - `created_at` (REAL NOT NULL): Epoch timestamp of creation.
   - `updated_at` (REAL NOT NULL): Epoch timestamp of latest message.
   - `metadata` (TEXT): JSON-encoded metadata.
   - Indices: `idx_conv_updated` ON `conversations(updated_at DESC)`, `idx_conv_person` ON `conversations(person_name)`.
2. `conversation_messages` Table:
   - `id` (TEXT PRIMARY KEY): Unique message identifier (`msg_<hex12>`).
   - `conversation_id` (TEXT NOT NULL): Foreign key referencing `conversations(id)` with `ON DELETE CASCADE`.
   - `role` (TEXT NOT NULL): Message sender role (`user`, `assistant`, `system`).
   - `content` (TEXT NOT NULL): Raw message content.
   - `provider` (TEXT): Provider that generated the response (`groq`, `ollama`, `openai`, `rule_based`).
   - `model` (TEXT): Exact model name used (e.g., `llama3.2:3b`, `qwen/qwen3.8-27b`).
   - `is_offline` (INTEGER DEFAULT 0): Binary flag indicating whether the message was processed offline (1) or online (0).
   - `timestamp` (REAL NOT NULL): Epoch timestamp.
   - `metadata` (TEXT): JSON-encoded message telemetry.
   - Indices: `idx_msg_conv` ON `conversation_messages(conversation_id, timestamp ASC)`.

