## CHAPTER 7: MULTI-CONVERSATION & PERSONAL CHAT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

### 7.1 Architecture of ConversationManager (`memory/conversation_manager.py`)
The `ConversationManager` class encapsulates all multi-session and multi-person logic:
- `create_conversation(title, person_name, system_prompt)`: Instantiates a new thread.
- `get_or_create_person_chat(person_name)`: Looks up whether an existing thread exists for a specific person (case-insensitive match on `person_name`). If found, returns that conversation; if not found, automatically creates a dedicated thread titled `"[Person] Chat"` with an empathetic personalized system prompt.
- `add_message(conv_id, role, content, provider, model, is_offline)`: Appends message to history and updates conversation's `updated_at` timestamp.
- `get_messages(conv_id, limit)`: Returns chronological history for isolated context injection.
- `rename_conversation(conv_id, new_title)`: Updates conversation title.
- `delete_conversation(conv_id)`: Deletes conversation and automatically cascades deletion to all associated messages.
- `search_messages(query, conv_id)`: Performs SQL `LIKE` search across message contents.

### 7.2 Strict Chat History Isolation Guarantee
To ensure privacy and contextual clarity:
- Messages belonging to a person chat (such as Kannaya) are strictly scoped to `conv_0b7e3df21e43`.
- When Iris thinks in another conversation (such as a Python programming chat or General Chat), only messages matching that active `conversation_id` are loaded into the LLM's context window.
- Personal facts and private exchanges never leak across separate topic threads.

### 7.3 REST Endpoints for Chat & Model Routing
Integrated directly into `backend/server/api.py`:
- `POST /chat`: Accepts `ChatRequest` containing `message`, `voice`, `conversation_id`, and `person_name`. Returns `ChatResponse` with `response`, `provider`, `model`, `is_offline`, and `conversation_id`.
- `GET /model/status`: Returns current connectivity (`online`/`offline`), active provider, active model, and list of installed Ollama models.
- `POST /model/select`: Switches routing mode (`auto`, `offline_only`, `online_only`) or locks preferred models.
- `GET /model/ollama/models`: Returns list of locally installed Ollama models.
- `GET /conversations`: Lists conversations ordered by latest activity with message counts and last message previews.
- `POST /conversations`: Creates a new general topic conversation.
- `GET /conversations/{id}`: Fetches conversation details and message history.
- `PUT /conversations/{id}`: Renames a conversation.
- `DELETE /conversations/{id}`: Deletes a conversation and its messages.
- `POST /conversations/person/{person_name}`: Creates or opens a dedicated person chat.

