## CHAPTER 8: HANDS AUTOMATION, APPLICATION LAUNCHING & SMART CONTROLLERS

### 8.1 Hands Execution Architecture (`hands/`)
The "Hands" subsystem gives Iris physical command of the Windows operating system:
- `AppLauncher` (`hands/app_launcher.py`): Scans Windows registry, Start Menu shortcuts, and PATH to launch installed applications (Chrome, VS Code, Spotify, Notepad, Calculator, Terminal, etc.) via `subprocess.Popen`.
- `TypoCorrector` (`core/typo_corrector.py`): Employs rapid Levenshtein distance and phonetic matching to correct misspelled voice or typed commands before execution (e.g., "opn chrom" -> "open chrome", "whatapp" -> "whatsapp").
- `SystemControl` (`hands/system_control.py`): Controls Windows master volume, screen brightness, lock workstation (`rundll32.exe user32.dll,LockWorkStation`), minimize all windows (`Shell.Application.MinimizeAll`), sleep, and shutdown.
- `TerminalExecutor` (`hands/terminal.py`): Executes administrative PowerShell and CMD commands with timeout controls and stdout capture.

### 8.2 WhatsApp Controller (`hands/whatsapp_controller.py`)
- Purpose: Automates WhatsApp messaging natively or via WhatsApp Web/Desktop.
- Capabilities: Locates contacts by name, prepares typed messages, executes dispatch, and verifies contact selection. Tested and verified via `scratch/test_select_contact.py`.

### 8.3 YouTube Controller (`hands/youtube_controller.py`)
- Purpose: Media playback and searching.
- Capabilities: Opens YouTube searches, initiates video playback, controls pause/play, volume adjustment, and full-screen toggling.

### 8.4 TodoManager & TodoScheduler
- Purpose: Manages Layer 2 memory tasks and reminders.
- Operation: `TodoScheduler` runs a background timer thread checking pending tasks against system time, triggering spoken alarm announcements through `VoiceEngine`.

