## CHAPTER 9: VISION SYSTEM, OCR & BIOMETRIC PRESENCE ENGINE

### 9.1 Camera Presence & Emotion Engine (`vision/presence_emotion.py`)
- Hardware Interface: Accesses local webcam via OpenCV (`cv2.VideoCapture(0)`).
- Face Detection: Detects user face presence using Haar cascades / dlib facial landmark meshes.
- Single-Owner Biometric Security Vault: Computes facial embeddings for "Commander". If an unauthorized individual sits in front of the terminal, Iris blocks system commands and issues a biometric warning.
- Real-Time Emotion Classification: Categorizes facial expressions into 6 states: `happy`, `sad`, `neutral`, `angry`, `surprised`, `focused`, adapting Iris's conversational tone and ThinkingOrb glow accordingly.

### 9.2 Screen Vision & OCR Engine (`vision/`)
- Screenshot Capture (`vision/screenshot.py`): Captures full-resolution or multi-monitor Windows desktop frames via Pillow/Win32 APIs.
- Frame Quality Sentinel: Classifies captured frames as `ok`, `blurry`, or `blank` (using Laplacian variance and Canny edge detection) before AI processing to prevent hallucinations on dark or covered screens.
- OCR Engine (`vision/ocr.py`): Performs optical character recognition extracting textual content, error messages, and window text directly from user screens.
- Multimodal Vision API (`/vision/see`): Dispatches frames to Gemini Flash (`gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-2.0-flash`) or OpenRouter to provide real-time screen commentary ("What's on my screen?").

