## 12. Multilingual Comprehension & Musical Sing-Along Intelligence

### 12.1 Omnilingual Comprehension & English Formulation Directive
- The core cognitive brain and model router have been upgraded to understand input in every human language and regional dialect:
  - Supports Hindi, Telugu, Tamil, Punjabi, Urdu, Spanish, French, German, Japanese, Chinese, Hinglish, and more.
  - Removes rigid language pinning in speech transcription, allowing Groq Whisper (`whisper-large-v3`) to perform automatic cross-language speech recognition.
  - Enforces a strict system prompt directive: IRIS comprehends the full emotional and linguistic nuance of the foreign input, but always reasons, formulates, and delivers its voice and text response in natural, fluent English (unless explicitly instructed by the user to speak in another language).

### 12.2 Music, Song & Lyric Perception Engine (`backend/intelligence/music_engine.py`)
- Dedicated intelligence subsystem specialized in recognizing music, spoken lyrics, hummed melodies, and vocal singing.
- Hybrid Two-Tier Perception:
  - Tier 1: Instant local catalog matcher executing high-performance regular expressions for iconic national and global hits across Hindi, Telugu, English, and Spanish in under one millisecond.
  - Tier 2: Deep LLM lyric extraction leveraging Groq and open language models to parse unknown or obscure song lyrics into structured metadata (song title, primary artist, composer, movie or album, original language, continuation lyrics, and cultural backstory).

### 12.3 Contextual Music Working Memory & Anaphoric Resolution
- Active Working Memory Window:
  - Automatically caches the most recently identified or discussed musical track with a five-minute time-to-live expiration.
- "Play It" Anaphoric Resolution:
  - Solves the natural speech problem where a user sings or discusses lyrics and subsequently issues a brief command such as "play it", "play this", or "just play the song".
  - Rather than falling back to generic top hits, the Decider, YouTube Controller, and Brain inspect the Music Engine's active working memory and automatically translate the pronoun into the exact song title and singer.

### 12.4 Musical Companion Dialogue & Sing-Along Interaction
- Interactive Companionship:
  - When the user quotes or sings lyrics, IRIS does not deliver dry technical search results. Instead, it acts as an enthusiastic musical companion.
  - Acknowledges the track, provides a short backstory or interesting fact about the movie or artist, and harmonizes with the user by reciting or singing the next one or two lines of the lyrics.
  - Concludes by proactively asking if the user would like the original track played on YouTube.

### 12.5 Direct YouTube Playback Integration
- When the user instructs IRIS to play the track, the task execution layer dispatches the command to the YouTube automation controller.
- The controller safely encodes the precise title and artist query, navigates to YouTube, and triggers instant playback in the background or active browser without interrupting the conversation state.


