## 16. Relational Persistence & Secure Authentication Architecture

### 16.1 Local Relational Database Pipeline & Connection Sanitization
- Local PostgreSQL 18 Engine Integration:
  - Configured persistent relational database storage targeting the local database repository (`iris_db`) running on standard workstation port fifty-four thirty-two.
  - Diagnosed and resolved the network address resolution exception (`getaddrinfo failed`). The fault originated from reserved symbol ambiguity when database credentials contain separator characters, resulting in malformed host parsing.
  - Implemented automatic connection string sanitization in the application settings configuration layer. The pipeline automatically ensures that reserved credential characters are URL-encoded before establishing the asynchronous database connection pool, preventing connection failures regardless of raw user input format.
  - Standardized local loopback resolution to explicit numeric IPv4 addressing to bypass Windows IPv6 resolution latency.

### 16.2 Modern Cryptographic Password Security
- Native Cryptographic Hashing Migration:
  - Replaced legacy hashing context wrappers with direct, modern bcrypt cryptographic processing.
  - Solved upstream library incompatibilities on modern Python environments where internal bug-detection routines overflowed maximum byte lengths.
  - Implemented boundary-safe string encoding enforcing proper byte limitations while preserving full entropy, guaranteeing rapid and deterministic authentication checks during registration and sign-in.

### 16.3 Relational Schema Initialization & Default Entitlements
- Automatic Relational Schema Provisioning:
  - Bootstrapped and verified all primary database entities within PostgreSQL: users, subscriptions, clones, and payment transaction logs.
  - Enforced transactional atomicity during user onboarding: account creation simultaneously provisions the primary identity record and registers a default active Free subscription tier in a single commit boundary.
  - Guarded against duplicate email registrations with clear and structured client feedback.

### 16.4 Subscription Elevation Security & Payment Guardrails
- Protected Entitlement Architecture:
  - Closed placeholder elevation loopholes that previously allowed paid tiers (such as Student Pro and Lifetime) to be activated through unverified direct client requests.
  - Restricted paid tier transitions strictly to verified payment confirmation webhooks from registered payment providers.
  - Preserved standard Free tier selection while guaranteeing that paid capabilities require confirmed billing events.
